{"api_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/6896","collected_at":"2026-09-27T21:56:47.573872+00:00","comments":[{"author_association":"COLLABORATOR","body":"The `This thread has been waiting for 5000ms for and may be stuck` message means that one of the other participants in `pmap` didn't show up to a collective operation like `psum` after a thread had been waiting for 5s. Now, this is sometimes benign: threads/GPUs are slow sometimes. The part that makes me think it's a real bug is that the GPU utilization then drops to 0 and stays there.\r\n\r\nThe question is: why is one device (presumably device `2`) getting stuck? One way this might happen if some computation before the collective is not terminating. Another way that it might happen is if you put collectives like `psum` in control flow, and not all participants are taking the same branches.\r\n\r\nIf nothing like that rings a bell, I think we'd need a reproduction to make further progress.","created_at":"2021-06-07T19:50:57Z","html_url":"https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/6896#issuecomment-856210393","id":856210393,"issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/6896","minimized":null,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDg1NjIxMDM5Mw==","performed_via_github_app":null,"pin":null,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/856210393/reactions"},"updated_at":"2021-06-07T19:50:57Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/856210393","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/348932?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hawkinsp/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hawkinsp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hawkinsp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hawkinsp/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hawkinsp","id"